From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hdmitx21: a VESA timing as YCbCr 4:4:4 when the sink takes it

1080p165, the frame-sequential 3D base, went out as RGB 8-bit like every
VESA timing. On S6 that RGB is made from the VPU's YCbCr by a matrix that
expands video levels to full range and uses BT.601, while the AVI frame
states limited range and BT.709: a TV that believes the frame shows the
picture crushed and dark.

A VESA timing now goes out as YCbCr 4:4:4 when the sink declares 4:4:4,
as the VPU makes it, so no matrix runs; with deep colour when the sink
takes deep colour in 4:4:4 and the driver's own check of the mode and
format passes (10-bit 1080p165 needs 501 MHz of TMDS clock). A sink without 4:4:4, or
an attr naming RGB, keeps RGB 8-bit. hdmitx21_set_display forces RGB on a
VESA timing only where DRM did not decide 4:4:4.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
@@ -421,12 +421,24 @@ static int meson_hdmitx_decide_color_att
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* VESA timings go out as RGB 8-bit (hdmitx21_set_display); decide it
-	 * here too, so the TMDS clock is worked out for what is sent
+	/* A VESA timing goes out as YCbCr 4:4:4, as the VPU makes it, when the
+	 * sink takes it, in deep colour where it takes that in 4:4:4 and the
+	 * link carries it; otherwise as RGB 8-bit
 	 */
 	if (vic >= HDMITX_VESA_OFFSET) {
-		attr->colorformat = HDMI_COLORSPACE_RGB;
-		attr->bitdepth = colordepth_to_bitdepth(COLORDEPTH_24B);
+		char attr_str[16];
+
+		if (attr->colorformat != HDMI_COLORSPACE_RGB &&
+		    (common->rxcap.native_Mode & (1 << 5))) {
+			attr->colorformat = HDMI_COLORSPACE_YUV444;
+			build_hdmitx_attr_str(attr_str, attr->colorformat, attr->bitdepth);
+			if (attr->bitdepth > 8 && (!common->rxcap.dc_y444 ||
+			    !hdmitx_common_chk_mode_attr_sup(outputmode, attr_str)))
+				attr->bitdepth = colordepth_to_bitdepth(COLORDEPTH_24B);
+		} else {
+			attr->colorformat = HDMI_COLORSPACE_RGB;
+			attr->bitdepth = colordepth_to_bitdepth(COLORDEPTH_24B);
+		}
 	}
 
 	DRM_INFO("[%s]:[%s,eotf:%d,vic:%d]=>attr[%s,%dbit]\n", __func__,
--- a/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hdmi_tx_video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx21/hdmi_tx_video.c
@@ -103,7 +103,9 @@ int hdmitx21_set_display(struct hdmitx_d
 	struct hdmi_format_para *param = &hdev->tx_comm.fmt_para;
 	int ret = -1;
 
-	if (videocode >= HDMITX_VESA_OFFSET) {
+	/* a VESA timing goes as YCbCr 4:4:4 where DRM decided it, else as RGB */
+	if (videocode >= HDMITX_VESA_OFFSET &&
+	    param->cs != HDMI_COLORSPACE_YUV444) {
 		param->cs = HDMI_COLORSPACE_RGB;
 		param->cd = COLORDEPTH_24B;
 		HDMITX_INFO("VESA only support RGB format\n");
